<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaties of Nijmegen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1678–1679</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Peace of Nijmegen, Treaty of Nijmegen · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franco-dutch-war">Franco-Dutch War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaties of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nijmegen">Nijmegen</a> ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franco-dutch-war">Franco-Dutch War</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>. Spain ceded Franche-Comté and a string of towns in the Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, including Cambrai, to France. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a> also kept his gains in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a>, where the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/free-imperial-city">free imperial cities</a> of the Decapolis passed under French rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaties-of-nijmegen.jpg" alt="Treaties of Nijmegen" width="320" height="193" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Henri Gascar · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vrede_van_Nijmegen_-_De_ondertekening_van_de_Vrede_tussen_Frankrijk_en_Spanje_door_Henri_Gascard_(1635-1701).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
